add(212,57,[272],[(57,'17–39')],'conjecture','Je conjecture','Three separate problems are posed: finite-order approximation of Picard images over a good henselian local ring; comparison under support of R¹f_*O at the closed point; and punctured-local Picard comparison near an isolated singularity.','The target of (ii) is uncertain. Artin approximation addresses finite-order approximation under explicit excellence/finite-presentation hypotheses; it does not by itself prove equality with the complete Picard group.','agrees','The note keeps the three questions and the conditional implication through resolution distinct.',[s57(12,'kept','Three independent completion questions are present; none is replaced by an unconditional comparison theorem.')])
add(213,57,[272],[(57,'18–39')],'idea of the earlier run','Cela doit être vrai aussi dans le cas analytique','An analytic-to-algebraic projectivity criterion in an unavailable earlier range is not proved here. The live sentence asks for an analytic analogue of the comparison questions.','The stronger if-and-only-if in Hua’s modernization is an earlier-run proposal; the external range and project files are unavailable.','agrees','P03 appropriately distinguishes a proposed sufficient condition from a recovered equivalence.',[s57(13,'kept','Retain only the weaker question this packet actually writes; quarantine the external modernization.')])
add(214,57,[275,279,280],[(57,'68–78,109–141')],'other','Néron-Severi','The quotient used for néronisation is Pic/Pic^τ. Over an algebraically closed field for a proper variety this removes the torsion in NS=Pic/Pic^0.','The distinction from Pic/Pic^0 is essential; fibrewise numerical equivalence is the stated relation.','agrees','P04 accurately notices the quotient’s torsion convention.',[s57(14,'kept','The quotient is explicitly by Pic^τ; identifying it with the full integral NS group would be wrong.')])
add(215,57,[275,276,277],[(57,'68–107')],'unproved claim','fidèlement plat','The fppf quotient Pic/Pic^τ is described by torsors/cosets; representability is related to existence of a faithfully flat quotient, and separatedness to closedness of the kernel.','A coset is an open subscheme of Pic, not of Pic^τ unless it is the identity coset. Finite-presentation and representability hypotheses must be retained.','understates','The note identifies descent and the finite-type question but does not flag the incorrect ambient Pic^τ in the literal coset sentence.',[s57(15,'corrected','Add the scan276 ambient-space alarm: nonidentity Pic^τ-cosets cannot lie inside Pic^τ; no ink correction is made.')])
add(216,57,[277],[(57,'92–107')],'conjecture','il suffirait','The margin hopes that flat closed Pic^τ suffices for representability of the Néron quotient, perhaps without representability of full Pic.','An algebraic-space quotient theorem is not automatically a scheme-representability theorem; keep the precise category in the open problem.','agrees','The weaker assertion is a live conjecture, separate from the preceding proper/quasiprojective sufficient setting.',[s57(16,'kept','P06 preserves the distinction between a stated sufficient setting and the stronger marginal conjecture.')])
