add(219,57,[284,285,286,287],[(57,'192–316')],'unproved claim','A′^Γ','For X=(A×B)/Γ with a free action on B and the specified action on A, the fixed subgroup scheme of the dual abelian scheme enters the Picard calculation. Its tangent space cannot be replaced by invariants of geometric points.','The displayed replacement of full Pic(A) by A′ requires a component restriction. The earlier-run finite-kernel reduction is conditional on the stated Albanese and equivariance hypotheses.','agrees','P10 correctly retains scheme structure, which is decisive in characteristic2.',[s57(20,'kept','The fixed subgroup scheme, not its reduced point set, controls the nonreduced example.')])
add(220,57,[314],[(57,'981–1004')],'unproved claim','ouvert et rétrocompact','For a proper flat finitely presented family, the fibrewise numerically trivial locus defines an open quasi-compact Picard subfunctor; the page also states closedness in the projective geometrically integral case.','The proof invokes numerical criteria (viii′b′) and (viiie), absent from this packet; these dependencies must be resolved externally.','agrees','P11 correctly records a proof with missing antecedent criteria rather than a self-contained argument.',[s57(21,'kept','Retain the theorem and its external numerical-criterion dependency.')])
add(221,57,[285],[(57,'233–249')],'unproved claim','Y′×{}_2A′','For the inversion/translation quotient by a constant group of order2 acting freely, the displayed Pic^τ factor is Y′×A′[2]. It is flat in the indicated abelian-scheme family, smooth when2 is invertible and non-smooth in characteristic2 when dimA>0.','The h¹(O)=dimA+dimB jump is the characteristic2 fibre calculation; it is not a nonflat Pic^τ example.','agrees','E01 makes this distinction, which the finite-flat kernel computation supports.',[s57(22,'kept','The example distinguishes flatness from smoothness; the characteristic qualification is essential.')])
add(222,57,[287,288],[(57,'291–320')],'self-flagged step','Il serait intéressant','The tangent/invariant formulas suggest searching for h^{0,1}−h^{1,0} of either sign and jumps in Hodge numbers. The next page lists four hoped-for pathologies but constructs none there.','Taking Γ-invariants is not exact in wild characteristic; the proposed comparison needs all action hypotheses.','agrees','E02 gives the formula and E03 correctly treats the four outcomes as a programme, not completed examples.',[s57(23,'kept','The Hodge-invariant expression is the source of the proposed examples.'),s57(24,'merged','The four-pathology announcement is the continuation of that same construction programme, not four established counterexamples.')])
add(223,57,[289,290],[(57,'322–368')],'unproved claim','divisible par p','The proposed homomorphism u:X/F→X/G is generically not p-divisible but becomes p-divisible on the special fibre; the corresponding NS specialization can have p-primary cokernel.','The literal pF=G clause and subsequent generic inclusion conflict with the claimed rank-p example. The conditional diagram argument works with pF⊂G and F_generic not contained in G_generic; a concrete elliptic realization is not silently certified.','understates','The notes notice subgroup/duality doubts; the equality pF=G is itself incompatible with nonzero G when pF=0.',[s57(25,'corrected','Add the explicit pF=G contradiction while retaining the conditional specialization mechanism.'),s57(26,'merged','E05 is the modern-literature comparison for the same p-divisibility phenomenon; Maulik–Poonen’s CM example is distinct.'),s57(40,'merged','D09 is the same distinction between torsion-free individual NS groups and nonsaturated specialization.')])
add(224,57,[294,297],[(57,'425–448,499–539')],'self-flagged step','Im u_μ ⊂ Im v','The first-order deformation discussion compares the obstruction to lifting line bundles with a cup product involving c₁ and a deformation class, and asks whether a p-divisible Picard part lifts.','The superscript00/∞ and cohomological degree1/2 are unresolved readings. Divisibility of points of Pic^0 over an algebraically closed field is not flatness of a subgroup scheme over a nonreduced base.','agrees','E06 and E07 explicitly keep pointwise group theory and infinitesimal deformation separate.',[s57(27,'kept','Pointwise p-divisibility cannot discharge the stated flatness/lifting issue.'),s57(28,'merged','The obstruction and μ₂ diagrams belong to the same unfinished deformation calculation.')])
add(225,57,[311],[(57,'919–933')],'conjecture','torsion','The page asks about variation of Néron–Severi torsion, separately from rank, and suggests an Igusa-type modular family.','The prime-to-characteristic specialization constraints of smooth proper families do not decide arbitrary p-primary torsion behavior.','agrees','E08 preserves the torsion/rank distinction and does not claim a constructed family.',[s57(29,'kept','The proposed family is a lead; the page only asks the torsion-continuity question.')])
add(226,57,[313],[(57,'950–979')],'conjecture','Oui par Raynaud','The questions concern separatedness and variation of the abelian, multiplicative and unipotent dimensions of Picard fibres; the final correspondence assertion is annotated affirmatively with Raynaud’s name.','The annotation is evidence of an answer known to the writer, not identification of an exact published theorem. The meaning of α,μ,λ and specialization hypotheses must be fixed.','agrees','E09 does not convert the attribution into a complete reference or suppress the preceding open inequalities.',[s57(30,'kept','Keep the several invariants and the attributed affirmative answer separate; no source is invented.')])
add(227,57,[315],[(57,'1005–1011')],'conjecture','se prolonge','Over a trait, a generically algebraically trivial line bundle is asked to extend with algebraically trivial special fibre. The page links an affirmative answer to representability and asks about representability under normal/integral-fibre hypotheses.','Extension of a class, extension of a chosen bundle and properness of a Picard component are different assertions. The crossed Raynaud attribution is not retained as a live theorem.','agrees','E10 preserves both extension requirements and the distinction from properness.',[s57(31,'kept','The note correctly keeps extension, specialization and representability as distinct questions.')])
add(228,57,[291,292],[(57,'370–423')],'other','T_p(M)=Hom(M,Q_p/Z_p)','For a p-primary torsion abelian group M with finite M[p], M is a finite p-group plus finitely many Prüfer groups. The written T_p is contravariant Hom(M,Q_p/Z_p), while T^p=lim M[pⁿ] is covariant.','This is abstract group theory, not the Dieudonné module of the full finite group scheme A[p].','agrees','D01 correctly retains the opposite variance and the distinction from Oda’s notation.',[s57(32,'kept','The variance distinction is explicit and mathematically indispensable.')])
