add(236,57,[298,300],[(57,'541–592,608–623')],'unproved claim','non quasi-affine','Two copies of A² minus the origin are identified along the punctured x-axis with x=t and x=t⁻¹. A global function restricts to both a polynomial in t and a polynomial in t⁻¹, hence is constant along the glued G_m; the resulting scheme cannot be quasi-affine.','The global function ring need not itself equal k: functions divisible by y remain. The obstruction is failure to separate points of the glued curve.','agrees','C01 correctly uses constancy on the glued curve rather than a false assertion that all global functions are constant.',[s57(41,'kept','The Laurent-polynomial restriction calculation proves the stated non-quasi-affineness.')])
