add(238,57,[302],[(57,'649–654')],'unproved claim','tous les faisceaux inversibles sont triviaux','Glue two projective spaces along a connected proper subscheme Y whose two hyperplane restrictions are Z-linearly independent in Pic(Y). The normalization is projective while the glued scheme has Pic=0 and is nonprojective, provided pushout existence and the global-unit exact sequence hold.','One concrete realization uses a complex elliptic curve with two degree3 line bundles differing by a nontorsion point. The unit quotient vanishes because k*×k*→k* is surjective.','agrees','C03 correctly says independence alone is insufficient without the units and existence checks.',[s57(43,'kept','The missing exact-sequence qualifications can be supplied by a precise pushout model; Ferrand6.3 matches the construction.')])
