add(281,58,[32],[(58,'444–477')],'other','1–9','The nine-part programme ranges from definitions and first consequences through depth, comparison, projective applications, purity and Lefschetz results.','These are nine planned topics, not a page count or evidence that each part survives in the supplied scans.','agrees','N11 accurately reads a programme, not nine finished theorems.',[n58(11,'kept','Keep the listed order as a guide to the packet’s internal organization.')])
add(282,58,[33],[(58,'478–547')],'other','(LG)_n','LG_n requires comparison for every vector bundle to be an isomorphism in degrees i≤n and injective in degree n+1. Weak LG is H⁰ comparison; LG includes neighborhood stability; effective LG asks that formal vector bundles algebraize on some neighborhood.','The categorical limit is a germ category over neighborhoods. These definitions must not be collapsed into one use of the word Lefschetz.','agrees','N12 correctly distinguishes degrees, neighborhoods and effectivity.',[n58(12,'kept','The four notions have different quantifiers and are retained separately.')])
add(283,58,[34],[(58,'548–571')],'self-flagged step','Oui','The weak-LG to LG_0 endpoint is supported by splitting extensions of vector bundles. The later suggestion that equality through degree n automatically gives injectivity in degree n+1 uses injective resolutions outside the tested vector-bundle class.','The n=0 Yoneda-extension argument is valid; the arbitrary-n generalization needs an acyclicity or effaceability theorem on the exact category.','agrees','N13 correctly separates the valid base case from the unsupported general endpoint.',[n58(13,'kept','Do not apply an injective-resolution argument whose terms are not vector bundles.')])
add(284,58,[34,35],[(58,'572–641')],'unproved claim','0→F→P→F′→0','If every vector bundle embeds in a finite direct sum of a generating family with locally free quotient, comparison in the two required degrees for the generators propagates by dimension shifting. For quasi-projective X the intended generators are sufficiently positive twists O(m).','The existence of these embeddings uses a resolution/ample-family hypothesis, not an arbitrary scheme.','agrees','N14 reads the proof’s exact-sequence mechanism and its hypothesis correctly.',[n58(14,'kept','The five-lemma argument is retained with finite sums and locally free cokernels explicit.')])
