add(294,58,[41,42,43],[(58,'874–975')],'withdrawn in the same text','Th2','The cancelled first permanence statement is reorganized as a coherent-sheaf theorem with relative flatness and proper support, followed by projective-flat corollaries.','Cancellation of the first draft is not rejection of permanence: the subsequent live text explicitly restates it.','agrees','N24 follows both locations.',[n58(24,'kept','Retain the reorganized live theorem and classify only the earlier draft as withdrawn.')])
add(295,58,[42],[(58,'884–936')],'reading question','plat relativement à Y|X','The base of flatness in the permanence theorem is unclear. The cohomological argument needs flatness over X for the usual proper-perfect pushforward approach, whereas flatness along Y can suffice only after a shrinking argument.','Which wording is written must be decided on the scan; both mathematical formulations remain distinguished.','agrees','N25 treats the base label as consequential.',[n58(25,'kept','The proof cannot choose X instead of Y silently.')])
add(296,58,[42,43],[(58,'884–975')],'idea of the earlier run','[Derived proof route is editorial.]','The earlier Hua run proposes using a bounded locally free model of Rf_*F for a projective morphism with F flat over a noetherian quasi-projective base and proper support, then applying the base comparison term by term.','This supports the cohomological permanence claim only after perfectness, derived base change and formal limit compatibility are justified. It does not alone algebraize a formal sheaf.','agrees','N26 explicitly describes a conditional modern route.',[n58(26,'kept','The proof route is retained with its exact missing hypotheses, separately from effectivity.')])
