add(298,58,[43],[(58,'937–975')],'conjecture','schémas projectifs et plats','The corollaries extend comparison/effectivity to projective flat schemes over the base; a margin suggests coherent modules with a faithfully flat module as auxiliary structure.','These categorical refinements have separate full-faithfulness and essential-surjectivity requirements.','agrees','N28 notices both the projective-scheme result and the proposed generalization.',[n58(28,'kept','Retain the two categorical assertions, with the generalization still qualified.')])
add(299,58,[42,43],[(58,'884–975')],'idea of the earlier run','un voisinage','For a coherent sheaf flat on the formal neighborhood and with proper support, the closed nonflat or nonfree locus has closed image in the base disjoint from Y; shrinking removes it under the stated finite-presentation assumptions.','This is a modern shrinking argument, not a proof that all hypotheses on proper support can be discarded.','agrees','N29 correctly uses properness to turn fibrewise information into a neighborhood statement.',[n58(29,'kept','Retain the closed-image argument and the finite-presentation/properness assumptions.')])
add(300,58,[44],[(58,'976–991')],'conjecture','omise','The author hopes some quasi-projectivity assumptions can be dropped, with uncertainty about the projective-scheme effectivity case.','Replacing quasi-projective by an arbitrary scheme requires a different resolution/algebraization input; the page gives none.','agrees','N30 accurately records an expectation and its exception.',[n58(30,'kept','Do not present removal of quasi-projectivity as a proved corollary.')])
