add(302,58,[46],[(58,'992–1066')],'conjecture','ρ est plein','For a punctured local spectrum P and its completion along D=V(t)∩P, completion kills coherent modules supported on closed sets disjoint from D, giving a faithful/conservative quotient functor. Fullness and the proposed essential image are stronger claims.','Faithfulness follows after quotienting by the exact kernel; unrestricted fullness is separately refuted in SA14-309.','agrees','N32 correctly separates the formal kernel quotient from the stronger assertions.',[n58(32,'kept','Retain the categorical claims as separate objects rather than using conservativity as evidence for fullness.')])
add(303,58,[46],[(58,'1018–1066')],'reading question','prof F_x≥2','The off-D depth condition and exclusions of associated cycles of small dimension are heavily revised; their exact scope governs the local comparison theorem.','The clean target-only Hom statement is isolated and checked in SA14-341; that result does not fix all the surrounding inequalities.','agrees','N33 recognizes the revisions instead of extracting a single arbitrary final condition.',[n58(33,'kept','Preserve the alternative dimension signs and the location of the depth condition.')])
add(304,58,[46],[(58,'1046–1066')],'unproved claim','Hom(F′,G′)','For finite modules over a noetherian local ring, depth Hom(F,G)≥min(2,depth G). Hence in a formal Hom comparison theorem the target depth often suffices, with no corresponding source-depth condition.','This local algebra inequality does not eliminate the complete-local/global hypotheses needed for the comparison theorem itself.','agrees','N34 correctly identifies the target-only mechanism.',[n58(34,'kept','The Hom-depth inequality is independently reproved and applied only in the verified setting.')])
add(305,58,[48],[(58,'1086–1136')],'self-flagged step','t non diviseur de0','The dévissage kills the stabilized t-power torsion K and replaces F by a quotient C on which t is regular; it then reduces formal comparison to a t-regular case.','The depth condition on the modification and the final Γ-comparison are incomplete; t-regularity alone is not formal comparison.','agrees','N35 keeps both the valid torsion reduction and the missing theorem.',[n58(35,'kept','The module calculation is valid, but the blank depth condition is not supplied.')])
