add(307,58,[50,52],[(58,'1181–1231,1275–1286')],'reading question','a), b), c′), T_1','The affine comparison corollary invokes conditions a,b,c′ and a set T₁ whose definitions are absent. A plausible c′ is extension of the formal sheaf to the whole completed affine scheme.','The undefined labels prevent identification of the full theorem; only explicitly recoverable subclaims are compared with literature.','agrees','N37 preserves the missing definitions rather than reconstructing a theorem by expectation.',[n58(37,'kept','Classify the full corollary as unidentified from these pages; keep the extension hypothesis only as a candidate.')])
add(308,58,[50,52],[(58,'1181–1231,1275–1286')],'unproved claim','i_*(F|U)','The proof tries to construct a coherent hull by direct image from an open U, controlling associated components and depth.','Direct image under an open immersion need not be coherent; the precise boundary condition and finite-generation theorem are essential.','agrees','N38 identifies the coherent-hull step rather than assuming it.',[n58(38,'kept','Retain the missing coherence criterion as a separate claim and problem.')])
add(309,58,[46],[(58,'992–1066')],'idea of the earlier run','ρ est plein','Unrestricted fullness fails for A=k[[x,y,z]], t=x, P=Spec A minus its closed point and F=G=O_{V(y)∩P}. With B=k[[x,z]], the quotient-category endomorphisms are B_(x), while the formal endomorphisms include k((z))[[x]]. The series Σ_{n≥0}z^{-n²}xⁿ lies only in the latter.','The denominator recurrence gives at most linear growth of z-pole orders for elements of B_(x). This example has depth1 at the closed point of P off D, so it does not refute the depth≥2 Hom theorem.','agrees','N39’s distinction between unrestricted fullness and the depth theorem survives independent checking.',[n58(39,'kept','The pole-order proof refutes the broad quotient claim but leaves the target-depth theorem intact.')])
add(310,58,[56],[(58,'1312–1383')],'other','a), a′), b), c)','The projective calculation poses four different questions: negative-twist vanishing, finite generation of positively graded cohomology, positive-twist vanishing, and formal comparison.','Their boundary and interior depth conditions differ; no one chain should be used to conflate them.','agrees','N40 supplies an accurate map of the four problems.',[n58(40,'kept','Keep all four questions separate in the claims and problem indexes.')])
add(311,58,[56],[(58,'1355–1370')],'reading question','α_i surjectif','In the exact localization sequence, surjectivity of H^{i−1}(X,F(−m))→H^{i−1}(U,F(−m)) is equivalent to injectivity of α_i:H_Z^i→H^i(X), not its surjectivity.','The correction is forced by exactness; it remains an ink-check candidate.','agrees','N41 identifies a direction error with a concrete exact-sequence test.',[n58(41,'kept','The proposed injectif reading is mathematically supported but not adopted.')])
add(312,58,[56,58,59],[(58,'1312–1383,1460–1565')],'unproved claim','Ext^{r−i}(F,ω_X)','Projective duality converts the α_i conditions into support/completion conditions on Ext^{r−i}(F,ω_X), and local duality then into depth statements.','All degree shifts, dualizations and negative twists are required; a support criterion is not a proof of an unrelated positive-grading condition.','agrees','N42 correctly recognizes the duality engine and its index sensitivity.',[n58(42,'kept','Retain exact degree r−i and both local/global dualities in the reconstruction.')])
add(313,58,[58],[(58,'1460–1528')],'unproved claim','module gradué de type fini','The claimed equivalence of positive graded finite generation and negative-twist vanishing is false. On P^r take F=k(p) at p outside the hyperplane Y and U=X. The positive section module is k[x₀], generated in degree0, but H⁰(F(−m))=k for every m.','Multiplication by the hyperplane equation is invertible on F; if a nonzero quotient is required, replace F by O_X⊕k(p).','agrees','N43’s counterexample checks grading, support and t-regularity.',[n58(43,'kept','Independent calculation confirms that the two finiteness assertions cannot be equated.')])
add(314,58,[58],[(58,'1506–1528')],'self-flagged step','lim H^i','Identifying formal cohomology with an inverse limit of cohomology of thickenings needs a Mittag–Leffler or derived-limit vanishing input.','The vanishing is not automatic for arbitrary inverse systems; proper finite cohomology or the precise finiteness theorem can supply it.','agrees','N44 correctly separates the inverse-limit step from the preceding comparison.',[n58(44,'kept','Record the actual formal-function/ML hypothesis instead of suppressing lim¹.')])
add(315,58,[58],[(58,'1506–1528')],'reading question','(*)','If the final condition (*) controls depth only near Z=X−U, it is vacuous for U=X and permits F=k(p) disjoint from Y. Then algebraic H⁰=k and formal H⁰=0, so the advertised comparison fails.','A stronger interior-depth or support condition is needed; the ambiguous star cannot be assigned a meaning merely to rescue the theorem.','agrees','N45 correctly ties the interpretation to a complete counterexample.',[n58(45,'kept','The star’s scope is a high-priority ink question; both interpretations are retained.')])
add(316,58,[59],[(58,'1529–1565')],'other','suffisantes, non nécessaires','The author explicitly distinguishes sufficient depth bounds for formal comparison from necessary conditions; the H⁰ case uses depth≥2 at the relevant closed points.','No converse depth theorem is extracted from this remark.','agrees','N46 faithfully preserves the logical strength of the page.',[n58(46,'kept','The sufficient criterion is not relabelled an equivalence.')])
add(317,58,[59],[(58,'1557–1565')],'reading question','F(−m|m)','The last restriction map changes the twist sign relative to the surrounding negative-twist calculation.','The consistent map should use the same twist on X and U; only scan inspection can determine the written sign.','agrees','N47 identifies a real source/target mismatch.',[n58(47,'kept','Retain a sign alarm rather than silently correcting the displayed target.')])
add(318,58,[60],[(58,'1566–1615')],'unproved claim','R^i g_*','The cohomological-finiteness criteria aggregate boundary local-cohomology conditions into coherence of R^i g_* and positive graded finite generation. The degree-zero term requires separate control of g_*F.','The identity R^i g_*≈H_Z^{i+1} holds for i>0; using it at i=0 discards the extension term.','agrees','N48 correctly identifies the endpoint issue.',[n58(48,'kept','Keep i=0 separate from the higher-direct-image equivalence.')])
add(319,58,[62],[(58,'1660–1705')],'unproved claim','F=g_*(F|U)','For i>0, positive-twist vanishing relates to R^i g_*=0 and local cohomology. The aggregate depth formulation additionally uses F=g_*(F|U), which kills the first two local-cohomology obstructions.','Dropping the hull equality changes the theorem.','agrees','N49 preserves the hypothesis written beside the equivalence.',[n58(49,'kept','The equality F=g_*F|U is structural and is retained in every modern restatement.')])
add(320,58,[56,58,59,60,62],[(58,'1312–1383,1460–1615,1660–1705')],'other','au voisinage de Z','Depth at points in U near the missing boundary and depth at points of Z are distinct conditions used for different cohomological problems.','One cannot replace one locus by the other without a coherent extension and a theorem connecting them.','agrees','N50 correctly summarizes the distinction revealed by the calculations.',[n58(50,'kept','The two depth loci remain explicit across the restatements.')])
add(321,58,[57,61],[(58,'1384–1459,1616–1659')],'other','Corollaire3.2','The repeated reused typescript is a formal-existence theorem and corollary; the two faces have different handwritten grading additions. A missing inequality before the depth2 bound remains a source blank.','The published match is SGA2 XII3.1–3.2; it clarifies the result but does not fill a literal missing typewriter sign.','agrees','N51 correctly keeps the two strata and the independent marginal material.',[n58(51,'kept','The SGA match is checked at the theorem level; neither face is discarded as an exact duplicate.')])
add(322,58,[47,49,51,53],[(58,'1067–1085,1137–1180,1232–1274,1287–1304')],'other','idéaux inversibles; algèbre extérieure','The reused sheets treat invertible fractional ideals as rank-one projective modules over a domain, determinants, homogeneous linear equations and the Jacobi cofactor identity.','These are ancillary algebra claims, each inventoried and computed where appropriate; they are not Lefschetz or Dieudonné theorems.','agrees','N52 correctly distinguishes the reused textual strata.',[n58(52,'kept','The displayed determinant identity is independently checked; the other statements retain their algebraic hypotheses.')])
add(323,58,[63],[(58,'1706–1753')],'other','Brauer-Witt','The reused representation-theory fragment states a decomposition criterion for group algebras using suitable hyperelementary subgroups (matrix algebras over their field centres, not necessarily split over the ground field); its character-induction formula is incomplete.','No Dieudonné comparison is established by the shared word module. The missing summation sign and undefined (R_p) remain source problems.','agrees','N53 recognizes the unrelated representation-theory topic.',[n58(53,'kept','Keep this as a truncated ancillary theorem, not a new Picard statement.')])
add(324,58,[65,67],[(58,'1754–1835,1967–2023')],'reading question','Ĉ=Spec S[z]','Scan65 writes Spec S[z], while scan67 explicitly calls Ĉ the projective cone. These are different schemes and have different Picard groups.','Proj S[z] is the candidate for the later projective-cone argument, but cannot replace the earlier written Spec without ink.','agrees','N54 correctly treats the construction symbol as decisive.',[n58(54,'kept','Keep both definitions and flag the conflict in Stage4.')])
add(325,58,[65],[(58,'1754–1835')],'reading question','Pic(C)=0 ??','The primed/tilde cone notation and boxed Picard-zero claims are not fully defined in the surviving page.','Only a precise affine graded-ring or projective-cone model can be tested; the undefined diagrams have classF in the claims map.','agrees','N55 declines to solve an unspecified object.',[n58(55,'kept','The boxed questions are retained without inventing their missing domains.')])
add(326,58,[65,67],[(58,'1754–1835,1967–2023')],'idea of the earlier run','Pic(C)=0','For a positively graded reduced seminormal finite-type k-algebra R with R₀=k, Pic(Spec R)=0 follows from Picard homotopy invariance and the grading contraction R→R[t].','Seminormality is an added modern sufficient hypothesis; it is not written into the doubtful boxed assertion.','agrees','N56 labels this as a conditional modern result.',[n58(56,'kept','The contraction proof is independently checked using Traverso3.6 under finite-normalization hypotheses.')])
add(327,58,[65,67],[(58,'1754–1835,1967–2023')],'idea of the earlier run','[Cusp test is editorial.]','A nonseminormal affine cusp tests failure of polynomial Picard invariance, but does not by itself refute Pic(X)→Pic(total space of a specified line bundle) for the projective X on scan67.','The ambient projective/full-section-ring hypotheses must be reproduced in any counterexample to that exact assertion.','agrees','N57 correctly limits the reach of an affine test case.',[n58(57,'kept','Retain the test as a warning about missing seminormality, not as a completed projective-cone counterexample.')])
add(328,58,[66],[(58,'1836–1857')],'reading question','H¹(X,O_X)','The surrounding multiplicative units exact sequence requires cohomology of O_X^*, so an unstarred H¹(X,O_X) would change additive cohomology into the Picard group incorrectly.','The missing star is a mathematical candidate only; the transcription is unchanged.','agrees','N58 identifies a category-changing symbol.',[n58(58,'kept','The unit/Picard sequence supports an O^* alarm, not an adopted reading.')])
add(329,58,[66],[(58,'1858–1884')],'unproved claim','factoriel ⇒ parafactoriel','Categorical parafactoriality requires both depth≥2 and Pic of the punctured spectrum equal to0. A DVR is factorial but fails this categorical condition because A^*→Frac(A)^* is not surjective.','With dimension≥2 and the appropriate noetherian normal/factorial hypotheses the familiar implication is restored.','agrees','N59 correctly detects the missing dimension/depth threshold.',[n58(59,'kept','The DVR refutes the unrestricted categorical implication; the repaired formulation is recorded separately.')])
add(330,58,[66],[(58,'1885–1966')],'unproved claim','g=1+Σg_i+Σn_s−ν','For a reduced connected proper curve over an algebraically closed field, the normalization sequence gives p_a=Σg_i+Σδ_s−ν+1. For a nodal curve this becomes Σg_i+b₁(dual graph).','The n_s must mean normalization-defect lengths, not merely numbers of branches. The nearby equation xy=0 in three variables defines a surface, not a curve.','agrees','N60 keeps the needed curve and defect interpretation explicit.',[n58(60,'kept','The normalization calculation is independently redone; the dimensional mismatch in the drawing stays a reading/interpretation alarm.')])
add(331,58,[66],[(58,'1885–1966')],'idea of the earlier run','[No tower theorem on the page.]','The equality between nodal graph cycle rank and a Picard torus rank is a finite-level geometric calculation; it does not establish a claim about pro-towers, derived functors or arithmetic reduction in another project.','External Dérivateurs/Longue Marche endpoints are unavailable and quarantined.','agrees','N61 correctly limits the project bridge.',[n58(61,'kept','Retain the numerical link only as a labelled external lead.')])
add(332,58,[67],[(58,'1967–2023')],'other','EGAII8.7.5,8.8.6','The cone calculation explicitly cites EGAII8.7.5 and8.8.6 for the cone/projective-bundle contraction. These are actual source cross-references, unlike inferred broad thematic links.','The published statements are checked with their full-section-ring and contraction hypotheses.','agrees','N62 distinguishes a genuine authorial reference from a retrospective analogy.',[n58(62,'kept','Keep both exact EGA locators and the cone model they require.')])
add(333,58,[67],[(58,'1967–2002')],'unproved claim','Pic Ĉ=Z','Under the stated projective/full-section-ring model with Γ(X,O_X)=k and a connected proper X, the blowup/projective-bundle model has Pic(X′)=Pic(X)⊕Z. Restriction to the exceptional section and descent of O(1) yield Pic(Ĉ)=Z if f_*O_{X′}=O_Ĉ.','The initially cancelled Pic(X′)=Pic(X) is not the final formula. The contraction and descent hypotheses are part of the conditional proof.','agrees','N63 tracks the correction and does not discard the extra Z summand.',[n58(63,'kept','Retain the conditional projective-cone result, with the corrected bundle formula and full section ring explicit.')])
add(334,58,[67],[(58,'2003–2023')],'conjecture','surjectif (?)','For the total space E of a line bundle over X, pullback Pic(X)→Pic(E) is split injective by the zero section. Surjectivity is queried. For reduced seminormal finite-type X it follows from affine Picard homotopy invariance and descent.','Seminormality is a sufficient modern hypothesis, not a claim that it is written or necessary for this particular bundle.','agrees','N64 correctly separates the elementary split injection from the unresolved surjection.',[n58(64,'kept','The zero-section calculation is exact; the sufficient seminormal theorem is proved separately.')])
add(335,58,[33,34,35],[(58,'478–641')],'idea of the earlier run','[No specific Fourier map.]','An old Koszul or exterior-power identity does not verify the actual Fourier comparison map in the unavailable cote47 packet.','The mathematical diagnostic is retained, but the external theorem and its proof are not declared inspected.','agrees','N66 already distinguishes a formal identity from the required map calculation.',[n58(66,'kept','Retain as an earlier-run methodological warning with quarantined endpoints.')])
