add(341,58,[46],[(58,'992–1066')],'unproved claim','Hom(F′,G′)→Hom( F̂′, Ĝ′)','Let A be a noetherian local quotient of a regular ring, complete for(t), t in its maximal ideal; let P be its punctured spectrum and D=V(t)∩P. If coherent G has depth≥2 at every point closed in P outside D, then Hom_P(F,G)→Hom_{P̂}(F̂,Ĝ) is an isomorphism for every coherent F.','This is the clean modern refinement of the strongest legible Hom claim. Raynaud1974I.1.1/1.3 supplies the comparison after checking the closure-dimension depth bounds; our proof records that reduction explicitly.','agrees','N79’s target-only conclusion is supported in this exact complete-local setting, not for the entire surrounding quotient category.',[n58(79,'kept','The precise Raynaud match and independent local-depth reduction confirm this clean Hom statement.')])
add(342,58,[42,43,46],[(58,'884–975,992–1066')],'idea of the earlier run','[P58 and L58 are register identifiers.]','The L58 clean Hom candidate is covered by a verified published theorem under the exact complete-local hypotheses. P58’s cohomological permanence has a modern proof route, while the full manuscript effectivity package and weakened hypotheses require separate identification.','A correction of an earlier register’s novelty status is local to the precise statement, not an assertion that every neighboring claim is known or that the original register was edited.','agrees','N80 distinguishes these scopes correctly.',[n58(80,'kept','Record the statement-level result and the remaining scope limits; no unavailable project file is changed.')])
add(343,58,[20,26,28,30,32,33,38,41,51,54,57,61,63],[(58,'1–37,238–288,324–547,710–991,1232–1274,1305–1459,1616–1659,1706–1753')],'title, date or page count','Applications aux morphismes projectifs et aux morphismes propres','The visible covers are Couples de Lefschetz-Grauert(X,Y) at28 and Applications aux morphismes projectifs et aux morphismes propres at54, with stated doubtful/deleted words. Other headings belong to internal sections or reused typescripts.','Rédaction numbers358,355,371 and programme1–9 are identifiers, not packet page totals.','agrees','The heading table is concordant with the supplied text, with all editorial uncertainty retained.',[s58(82,'kept','All listed headings are checked against their own textual strata; no external title replaces the covers.')])
add(344,58,['20–67'],[(58,'1–2023')],'title, date or page count','[No authorial total.]','The packet contains44 supplied faces in the scan range20–67 with omissions29,45,55,64. Scan identifiers, internal folios, printed pagination, rédaction numbers and corner numerals are separate systems.','The count44 is a delivery count, not an authorial statement; no date is inferred from corner numbers.','agrees','The pagination table correctly separates those systems.',[s58(83,'kept','Retain the supplied-face count as editorial metadata, without turning it into a manuscript page-total claim.')])
add(345,58,['20–67'],[(58,'1–2023')],'other','[Published reference list.]','The earlier notes’ bibliography is a source-discovery list. This consolidation independently opens the primary sources it relies on and records exact theorem locators, access failures and hypothesis mismatches.','A bibliography entry in the earlier notes is not itself a check event. Sources not opened in this run are not marked verified.','agrees','The bibliography is retained as a lead; the checked reference file supplies current verification status.',[s58(84,'kept','Retain its bibliographic role while independently auditing every result used here.')])
